x264_ssim oracle: accumulate in double (chapter 9 section 9.4.4, WI-3.308a). Applied by CMake with
-DOVT_X264_SSIM_DOUBLE_ACCUM=ON to a copy of the sources, `patch -p1`. x264 computes the per-window quotient, the
row sums and the plane mean in float, which is off from the spec's double definition by up to ~1.5e-6 per frame on the
Netflix pair; the spec definition is what ssim_x264 implements. For the 10-bit float branch only the quotient and the
sums change; the float window terms are kept.

--- a/pixel_ssim.c
+++ b/pixel_ssim.c
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@
